# Chroma library, modern Earth: the production sphere's events as they touch a life (Library thread, 2026-10-09, "v22"
# update stage 4, item 15 phase 3). Design: chroma-ideas/spheres-implementation.md sections 2, 4 "Library" and 5; data:
# chroma-ideas/spheres-data/prod.json (events with on_character and the modern epoch; each scene is built on the
# event's wording.modern and on_character). Face words: chroma-library/earth_spheres.py. Fields: build.py.
#
# Every moment here is an event moment: a life event the Engine fires on its sphere event (sphere_event: <key>) for the
# people its selector names (place or staff); per_year is all 0 and there are no drivers. The '# world:' line above
# each moment gives the event key, the selector and the share of selected people who meet the moment (estimate).
# Fourteen moments, one per prod event of the modern epoch that has on_character, except four that existing moments
# already answer: rich_season ('a bumper harvest'), lean_year ('a dry year on the land'), new_tool ('the machines come
# for the work', 'new technology changes your job') and heir ('a parent asks you to take over the family shop', 'a chance
# to start a business of your own', 'the owner wants to retire'). first_fields has no modern wording. Two moments are
# written at an angle the existing ones leave open: walkout is the strike in its third week (the ballot is 'a strike
# vote at work'), and drift_to_town is the valley emptying for every young person (the shadow moment 'a door out of
# town' is gated to those stuck in their ways). Tone follows the event's tone: 5 joy, 4 trouble, 5 mixed.
#
# Options: sphere: on each is the face the act is in (one-colour X: prod.X; a pair: its pair face in wheel order, so
# WR is prod.RW, WG prod.GW, UG prod.GU). Levers (lever:) where the act plainly is one, from character.levers.
# Accidents stay off-page: people are hurt, nobody dies on the page.
#
# Layout: each a life event with the five one-colour options and one pair set. The 14 use all twelve halves of D1 to
# D6, two of them twice (D2a, D4b), each chosen to hold the event's own pair faces where it has them (walkout and
# accident RW, land and coop GW, closed_season GW and GU, scarce_hands RG, name_won WU and RG, rush and venture BR).
# Evenness: in every moment each colour's one-colour chance plus half its two pairs' chances is the same sum, so every
# colour has the same mean chance in each moment and in every stage. No flags.
#
# share: on every moment (2026-10-10, Engine phase 3a) is its '# world:' share: the engine draws at birth who can
# ever meet it, so when the event comes to town only that share of the people there are open to the moment.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- rush (pairs D5b)

# world: sphere event rush, selector place, share .4
== the metal under the hills
tier: life event
sphere: prod
sphere_event: rush
share: .4
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-85
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 15-40
times: World event: rush (sphere prod). Selector place: a rich find or new ground opens and prices make it worth the trip; about 4 in 10 of the people living there meet it as a choice of their own, to go, to sell, to stay or to watch kin go (share .4, estimate), once in a life for most who meet it at all (estimate)
likelier: a find near home, a family with land, young people out of work, high prices for what is found
rarer: a town far from any find, secure work, older age
tone: mixed
life: work, money, family
horizon: years
roles: sibling, parent, friend
earth: a metal the new batteries need is found under the hills, rents triple in a year, and the old ranchers sell out or dig in
scene: Surveyors have found a metal under the hills that the new batteries need. In a year the rents in {place} have tripled, the mine is hiring at double pay, and the old ranchers are selling out or digging in. {sibling} has already signed on.
scene W: The mine hires anyone, fast, and the safety talk lasts ten minutes. {N} has heard what happens to rush towns with no rules.
scene U: {N} wants to know how deep the seam runs and how long the price will hold. Every rush ends.
scene B: Land that was worth nothing a year ago is worth a fortune now. {N} can see who will get rich, and how.
scene R: Double pay, a camp full of strangers, and the whole town awake at night. {N} wants in.
scene G: The ranch has been in the family for four generations. A company man has left an offer on the kitchen table and says it will not be made twice.
- W | ask the town meeting to set one fair rent for every new hand in the camp | v: universalism, benevolence | lever: voice | pushes: place | sphere: prod.W | chance: 69
- U | work out how long the seam will last, then decide what to stake on it | v: self-direction, security | sphere: prod.U | chance: 73
- B | lease your field to the company at the new price, and bank every payment | v: achievement, power | sphere: prod.B | chance: 72
- R | sign on at the mine for double pay and the nights in the camp | v: stimulation, hedonism | mark: took a wild risk | sphere: prod.R | chance: 65
- G | dig in on the ranch, and let the company build round you | v: tradition, security | mark: turned down a chance | lever: loyalty | pushes: place | sphere: prod.G | chance: 68
- BR | work double shifts for a year, spend freely, and get out before the bust | v: hedonism, achievement | sphere: prod.BR | chance: 56
- RG | guide the prospectors over the hills you know by heart, for a fee | v: self-direction, stimulation | sphere: prod.RG | chance: 72
- UG | count the springs on the old range, and show the council what the digging does | v: universalism, tradition | lever: voice | pushes: nature | sphere: prod.GU | chance: 50
- WB | open a boarding house for the new hands, with fair rent and clean beds | v: benevolence, achievement | lever: found | sphere: prod.WB | chance: 58
- WU | get yourself trained as the mine's safety inspector | v: security, achievement | lever: office | sphere: prod.WU | chance: 62
works: The boom lasts long enough, and {N} comes out of it with money put by and the family still talking.
works: When the mine winds down years later, {N} is one of the few who saw it coming and is ready.
fails: The price falls in the third year, the camp empties, and the rents stay high.
fails: {sibling} comes home from the mine with a bad back and less money than they went with.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- works_close (pairs D2b)

# world: sphere event works_close, selector place, share .6
== the plant moves its line abroad
tier: life event
sphere: prod
sphere_event: works_close
share: .6
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-85
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 10-30
times: World event: works_close (sphere prod). Selector place: a slump, cheaper goods from elsewhere or the owner's choice closes the town's works; about 6 in 10 of the people living there lose work themselves or through a parent, a partner or a friend (share .6, estimate), once or twice in a life in a works town (estimate)
likelier: a town with one big employer, a family that has worked there for years, a slump
rarer: a town of many small firms, work in a trade the closure does not touch
tone: trouble
life: work, money, community
horizon: years
roles: parent, friend, colleague
earth: the plant is moving its line abroad, and with its eight hundred jobs go the café opposite, the parts supplier and the late bus
scene: The plant is moving its line abroad. Eight hundred jobs go by the summer, and with them the café opposite the gates, the parts supplier and the late bus. {parent} has worked there for twenty-six years.
scene W: {N} thinks of the older hands who will never be hired again. Somebody should make sure they get everything they are owed.
scene U: The firm says the plant lost money. {N} wants to see the figures, and what the line would need to stay.
scene B: The old machines will be sold off cheap, and the plant's customers still need what they made. {N} sees a gap.
scene R: {N} feels the anger in every bar in town. Somebody should block the gates before the lorries take the line away.
scene G: Three generations of the family have clocked in at those gates. {N} cannot picture the town without them.
- W | help the older hands claim every payment and pension they are owed | v: benevolence, universalism | mark: helped someone in need | sphere: prod.W | chance: 75
- U | train for a trade that is hiring, at the college in the next town | v: achievement, self-direction | mark: learned a skill | sphere: prod.U | chance: 55
- B | buy two old machines at the auction, and take orders from the plant's customers | v: achievement, power | lever: found | sphere: prod.B | chance: 66
- R | leave for the city, where the work is, and do not look back | v: self-direction, stimulation | mark: moved away | lever: exit | sphere: prod.R | chance: 64
- G | stay and scrape by, so the family is still here when work comes back | v: tradition, security | mark: stayed home | lever: loyalty | pushes: place | sphere: prod.G | chance: 47
- RG | fix the neighbours' cars and boilers by hand in your garage, a job at a time | v: self-direction, security | sphere: prod.RG | chance: 64
- UB | find out who is buying the line, and sell them what only you know about it | v: achievement, power | sphere: prod.UB | chance: 48
- UG | write down how the old line ran, so the skill is not lost with the plant | v: tradition, universalism | sphere: prod.GU | chance: 64
- WB | put your payout into a small firm that hires the old crew | v: benevolence, achievement | lever: fund | pushes: place | sphere: prod.WB | chance: 42
- WR | join the hands blocking the gates on the day the lorries come for the line | v: universalism, self-direction | mark: defied an authority | lever: voice | pushes: institution employer | sphere: prod.RW | chance: 30
works: A small firm grows in the empty units, and {N} has work again, or a friend does, within a year.
works: The town is poorer, but {N} finds a way to make a living and stay among people {N} knows.
fails: The gates are chained by autumn, and the high street empties shop by shop.
fails: {parent} never finds work again, and the family's evenings grow quiet and hard.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- walkout (pairs D3a)

# world: sphere event walkout, selector staff, share .7
== the third week on the picket line
tier: life event
sphere: prod
sphere_event: walkout
share: .7
at: union
stages: young_adult adult mature
age: 18-67
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 5-20
times: World event: walkout (sphere prod). Selector staff: the hands walk out when pay falls behind prices, is cut, or after an accident or an insult on the floor; about 7 in 10 of the staff face the choice to stay out or go back in as their own (share .7, estimate), once or twice in a working life where the trade is organised (estimate); the ballot before it is 'a strike vote at work'
likelier: an organised trade, prices rising faster than pay, a firm that cuts, an accident on the floor
rarer: a small firm with no union, a year of rising pay, a trade where hands are easy to replace
tone: mixed
life: work, money, friends
horizon: months
roles: boss, colleague, friend, parent
earth: the strike is three weeks old, the managers run a skeleton shift, and your boss rings to ask whether you will come back in
scene: The union called the strike when the offer fell short of prices, and the gates have been picketed for three weeks. The managers run a skeleton shift, the strike pay is thin, and on Monday {boss} rang to ask whether {N} would come back in.
scene W: The vote was fair, and the strike is the crew's choice. {N} gave a word at that vote, and the crew is counting on it.
scene U: {N} has worked out what the offer is worth against prices, month by month. The gap is smaller than the speeches say.
scene B: {N} has a loan on the house and a family to feed. The firm has hinted that those who come back now will be remembered.
scene R: The fire in the brazier, the songs, the cars that sound their horns as they pass. {N} has never felt so alive at work.
scene G: {Ns} {parent} stood at the same gate in another strike, years ago. {N} knows that how the crew ends this matters for a long time.
- W | keep your word to the crew, and stand your shifts at the gate | v: conformity, benevolence | mark: kept your word | lever: voice | pushes: institution employer | sphere: prod.W | chance: 89
- U | show the crew what the offer is worth against prices, month by month | v: universalism, self-direction | sphere: prod.U | chance: 80
- B | go back in on the skeleton shift, and take the overtime | v: security, achievement | mark: made an enemy | sphere: prod.B | chance: 71
- R | keep the brazier going every night, and lead the songs at the gate | v: stimulation, benevolence | sphere: prod.R | chance: 79
- G | bring the young hands to the gate, and tell them how the last strike was won | v: tradition, benevolence | sphere: prod.G | chance: 64
- BG | take cleaning work across town to see the family through, and say so openly | v: security | sphere: prod.BG | chance: 70
- RG | spend the strike weeks mending the neighbours' roofs and fences for food and favours | v: benevolence, self-direction | sphere: prod.RG | chance: 72
- UB | find out quietly how long the firm can run on the skeleton shift | v: power, achievement | sphere: prod.UB | chance: 58
- WR | stand in the road in front of the bus that brings the skeleton shift in | v: universalism, self-direction | mark: defied an authority | lever: voice | pushes: institution employer | sphere: prod.RW | chance: 40
- WU | join the union team that checks the firm's books and drafts a fair counter-offer | v: universalism, achievement | lever: voice | pushes: institution employer | sphere: prod.WU | chance: 52
works: The firm gives way, the strike ends with a raise that beats prices, and {N} walks back in with the crew.
works: Whatever was done, {N} comes out of the strike with a friend made at the gate for life.
fails: The strike ends with little won, and some at the gate never speak to {N} again.
fails: The weeks without pay eat the savings, and the family feels it for a year.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- accident (pairs D1a)

# world: sphere event accident, selector staff, share .5
== the scaffolding comes down
tier: life event
sphere: prod
sphere_event: accident
share: .5
stages: young_adult adult mature
age: 18-67
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 10-30
times: World event: accident (sphere prod). Selector staff: dangerous work with thin safety, likelier when output is pushed; about half of the staff of the site or works feel it as their own, a colleague hurt and a choice to speak up, stay or leave (share .5, estimate), once or twice in a working life in a dangerous trade, many never (estimate)
likelier: building, mining, fishing or heavy industry, a firm that pushes the pace, warnings ignored
rarer: office work, a firm with a strong safety record, a strong union on the site
tone: trouble
life: work, health, friends
horizon: months
roles: colleague, boss, friend
earth: the scaffolding on the site collapses, the papers run the story for a week, and the union says it warned the company twice
scene: The scaffolding on the site came down on Tuesday morning. {colleague} is in hospital, badly hurt, and two others with them, and the union says it warned the company twice. The papers run the story for a week; the site reopens on Monday.
scene W: There were rules for that scaffold, and someone skipped them. {N} wants it said plainly, so it does not happen again.
scene U: {N} looked at those clamps the week before. Something about them was wrong, and {N} wants to know what.
scene B: The firm has offered a bonus to everyone who finishes the job on time. Nobody is saying the word inspection.
scene R: {N} was ten metres away. Every time a pole clangs, {Ns} heart jumps, and a voice says walk away from this trade.
scene G: {colleague} has three children at home. Someone has to look after the family while the hospital does its work.
- W | give the inspectors a full statement of everything you saw on the site | v: universalism, conformity | lever: voice | pushes: institution employer | sphere: prod.W | chance: 79
- U | photograph the clamps and the failed joints before the firm clears them away | v: self-direction, universalism | sphere: prod.U | chance: 70
- B | finish the job on time, take the firm's bonus, and keep your head down | v: achievement, security | sphere: prod.B | chance: 68
- R | walk off the site for good, and find work in another trade | v: self-direction, security | lever: exit | sphere: prod.R | chance: 78
- G | visit your colleague's family every week with food and news from the site | v: benevolence | mark: helped someone in need | sphere: prod.G | chance: 65
- BG | go back on Monday, and check every clamp you climb on yourself | v: security | sphere: prod.BG | chance: 66
- BR | sign on with a better-paid crew on a safer site across town | v: achievement, security | lever: exit | sphere: prod.BR | chance: 58
- UG | teach the young hands on the site how to check a scaffold before they climb | v: benevolence, security | sphere: prod.GU | chance: 64
- WR | refuse to climb, and get the crew to stop work until the scaffold is checked | v: security, universalism | mark: defied an authority | lever: voice | pushes: institution employer | sphere: prod.RW | chance: 46
- WU | stand as the site's safety rep, with the right to stop the job | v: security, universalism | lever: office | sphere: prod.WU | chance: 56
works: The inquiry backs the crew, the firm is fined, and the new scaffold is checked every morning.
works: {colleague} walks again by the summer, and knows who stood by the family.
fails: The firm blames a worn part, nobody is charged, and the site slips back to the old ways within a month.
fails: {N} cannot climb a ladder without shaking for the rest of the year.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- land_taken (pairs D1b)

# world: sphere event land_taken, selector place, share .3
== the last family farm in the valley
tier: life event
sphere: prod
sphere_event: land_taken
share: .3
haunt: prod.land
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-90
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 15-40
times: World event: land_taken (sphere prod). Selector place: land grows valuable, a strong buyer and a rule that backs the new owners; about 3 in 10 of the people living there are in a farm family that gets the offer or works its land (share .3, estimate), once in a life where it happens at all (estimate)
likelier: a small family farm, a valley where a big firm is buying, debts on the land
rarer: a town job, a farm with no debts and many heirs who want it
tone: trouble
life: family, work, home
horizon: years
roles: grandparent, parent, sibling
earth: a big farming firm buys out the neighbours one by one, and the last family farm in the valley gets an offer it can hardly refuse
scene: A big farming firm has bought out the neighbours one by one. The family farm is the last one left in the valley, and on Friday the firm's offer came: more than the land has ever earned, and a job managing it for the firm.
scene W: The valley always shared the harvest work, farm to farm. Now the firm brings in its own crews, and nobody knows them.
scene U: {N} has worked the numbers. The firm farms bigger and cheaper, and a small farm cannot match it for long.
scene B: The offer is good, and offers like it do not come twice. {N} could buy a smaller farm somewhere else and still be ahead.
scene R: {N} hates being told what the land is worth by a man who has never dug it.
scene G: {grandparent} planted the orchard behind the house. {N} cannot imagine selling the trees.
- W | take the offer only if the firm keeps on every hand who works the farm | v: benevolence, universalism | sphere: prod.W | chance: 73
- U | work out what the farm could earn with new crops, then answer | v: self-direction, security | sphere: prod.U | chance: 64
- B | bargain the offer up, sell, and buy a smaller farm in another valley | v: achievement, power | lever: exit | sphere: prod.B | chance: 68
- R | tell the firm's agent to get off the land, and mean it | v: self-direction | mark: made an enemy | sphere: prod.R | chance: 55
- G | turn the offer down, and keep the farm for the children | v: tradition | mark: turned down a chance | lever: loyalty | pushes: place | sphere: prod.G | chance: 58
- RG | keep the orchard worked by hand, and sell the fruit at the farm gate | v: self-direction, tradition | sphere: prod.RG | chance: 66
- UB | find out what the firm truly needs your land for, and price it to match | v: power, achievement | sphere: prod.UB | chance: 48
- UR | turn the farm into something the firm cannot copy, a cider press or a farm shop | v: self-direction, stimulation | lever: found | sphere: prod.UR | chance: 44
- WB | buy the neighbour's last field before the firm can, and hire their hands | v: power, benevolence | sphere: prod.WB | chance: 36
- WG | get the last farmers to pool their land and farm it together | v: universalism, tradition | lever: found | pushes: place | sphere: prod.GW | chance: 38
works: The farm stays in the family another generation, smaller in what it earns and larger in what it means.
works: {N} sells well, and makes a new start without bitterness.
fails: The firm's fences go up round the farm, the water rights go first, and the offer is lower next year.
fails: The family splits over the offer, and {grandparent} stops speaking to {N}.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- land_shared (pairs D5a)

# world: sphere event land_shared, selector place, share .4
== a title to the fields your family worked
tier: life event
sphere: prod
sphere_event: land_shared
share: .4
haunt: prod.land
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 14-95
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 20-60
times: World event: land_shared (sphere prod). Selector place: a land reform after unrest, a dearth or an empty countryside gives the land to those who work it; about 4 in 10 of the people living there are in a family that gets a title or loses one (share .4, estimate), once in a life where it happens at all (estimate)
likelier: a family of tenants or farm hands on a great estate, a reform government, years of unrest on the land
rarer: a town family, a family that owned land already, a place with no great estates
tone: joy
life: family, work, home
horizon: years
roles: grandparent, parent, sibling
earth: the land reform passes, the great estates are split, and your family receives a title to the fields it worked
scene: The land reform has passed. The great estate where {Ns} family has worked for three generations is being split, and the clerk at the town hall has a title with the family name on it: four fields, a barn and the right to the well.
scene W: Not every family on the estate gets a field. {N} thinks of the day labourers who were left off the list.
scene U: Four fields, and no one in the family has ever chosen what to plant. {N} wants to get it right.
scene B: Land of their own at last. {N} is already looking at the next field over.
scene R: No more foreman. {N} can work the fields to {Ns} own hours, and that alone feels like flying.
scene G: {grandparent} worked those fields for another family for sixty years. Now they will pass to the children.
- W | ask the land office to put the day labourers on the list too | v: universalism, benevolence | lever: voice | pushes: state | sphere: prod.W | chance: 70
- U | test the soil in each field, and plan the first crops on paper | v: self-direction, achievement | mark: learned a skill | sphere: prod.U | chance: 69
- B | borrow against the title for seed, tools and the next field over | v: achievement, power | mark: took a wild risk | sphere: prod.B | chance: 62
- R | plant what you always wanted to grow, and work the hours you choose | v: self-direction, hedonism | sphere: prod.R | chance: 77
- G | hold a family supper in the barn, and give the old hands the first toast | v: tradition, benevolence | sphere: prod.G | chance: 62
- BG | sell the far field to clear the family's debts, and farm the rest well | v: security | sphere: prod.BG | chance: 66
- UB | learn which crop the town will pay most for, before the neighbours do | v: achievement, power | sphere: prod.UB | chance: 66
- UR | try a crop nobody in the valley has grown, on one field | v: stimulation, self-direction | sphere: prod.UR | chance: 52
- WG | share the plough and the harvest work with the families on either side | v: benevolence, universalism | sphere: prod.GW | chance: 66
- WR | stand with the families whose titles the old estate is fighting in court | v: universalism, benevolence | lever: voice | pushes: state | sphere: prod.RW | chance: 50
works: The first harvest on the family's own land comes in, and {N} remembers it for the rest of {Ns} life.
works: The fields feed the family, and something is put by for the first time in years.
fails: The first year is dry, the loan comes due, and the title is pledged before it is a year old.
fails: The old estate's lawyers drag the titles through the courts for years.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- stock_fails (pairs D6a)

# world: sphere event stock_fails, selector place, share .6
== the boats tied up in the harbour
tier: life event
sphere: prod
sphere_event: stock_fails
share: .6
haunt: prod.wild
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 15-90
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 20-60
times: World event: stock_fails (sphere prod). Selector place: years of taking more than grows back, then a bad year tips it; about 6 in 10 of the people of a fishing, forest or herding town feel the family trade lose its living (share .6, estimate), once in a life where it happens at all (estimate)
likelier: a fishing or herding family, a town that lives by one stock, years of big catches
rarer: a town job, a family with another trade to fall back on
tone: trouble
life: work, family, money
horizon: years
roles: parent, friend, sibling
earth: the fish stock collapses, the fishery is closed for ten years, and the harbour town's boats are tied up overnight
scene: The fish stock has collapsed. The fishery is closed for ten years, and overnight every boat in the harbour of {place} is tied up. {parent} has fished these waters since leaving school.
scene W: The closure binds every boat the same, and {N} thinks it has to. But some crews will slip out at night regardless.
scene U: The scientists warned for years. {N} wants to see their counts, and to know whether ten years is enough.
scene B: A boat tied up for ten years is worth almost nothing. A boat sold now, to a buyer up the coast, is worth something.
scene R: {N} has never wanted any work but the sea. The thought of an office makes {N} want to shout.
scene G: Four generations of the family fished from this harbour. {N} wonders what will be left to hand on.
- W | keep the closure, and report the boats that slip out at night | v: conformity, universalism | sphere: prod.W | chance: 76
- U | sign on with the scientists to count the fish through the closed years | v: universalism, achievement | sphere: prod.U | chance: 74
- B | sell the boat up the coast now, while it still fetches a price | v: security, achievement | sphere: prod.B | chance: 60
- R | crew on a boat in a fishery far away, and send money home | v: stimulation, self-direction | mark: moved away | lever: exit | sphere: prod.R | chance: 78
- G | keep the boat painted and ready for the day the fishery opens again | v: tradition | lever: loyalty | pushes: place | sphere: prod.G | chance: 63
- BG | strip the old boats for engines and timber, and sell what can be sold | v: security, achievement | sphere: prod.BG | chance: 78
- UG | learn to farm shellfish in the bay, where the water is still healthy | v: self-direction, tradition | mark: learned a skill | sphere: prod.GU | chance: 54
- UR | refit your boat to take visitors out to see the seals | v: stimulation, self-direction | lever: found | sphere: prod.UR | chance: 56
- WB | lend the crews out of work enough to see them through the first winter | v: benevolence, power | lever: fund | sphere: prod.WB | chance: 60
- WR | lead the crews to the harbour office to demand help for the families | v: universalism, benevolence | lever: voice | pushes: state | sphere: prod.RW | chance: 46
works: {N} finds a living by the sea that does not need the fish, and stays.
works: Ten years on the counts are rising, and {N} is on the quay when the first boat goes out again.
fails: The harbour empties of young people, and {N} spends the winters watching the boats rot.
fails: Crews fish the closed waters at night, and the town turns on itself over who is cheating.

